{%- comment -%}
  THE product card. One shape, every listing: the collection grid, the collection
  "you may also like" rail, the product page's "More in ..." rail and the gift
  voucher rail all render this and nothing of their own.

  Until 1 Oct 2026 this card existed as seven hand-copied versions and the copies
  drifted — see MAINTENANCE.md, "Components get pasted, not shared". Four of them
  are now this file. The two that are not, and why:
    - sections/sale-products.liquid, the homepage Sale rail. A deliberately
      different design: centred, no vendor line, a fixed image height.
    - the compact ROWS, which are not this card at all: the search results page,
      the predictive-search dropdown, the cart drawer and the product page's own
      side list.
  Before adding a fifth copy, render this.

  Accepts:
    product  (required)
    width    optional flex-basis for a rail card, e.g. '254px'. Omit it inside a
             grid, where the grid track sets the width.

  Layout rules that matter, all of them in .prodcard* in base.css:
    - The title clamps to two lines with an ellipsis. It is clamped in CSS, not in
      Liquid, so the DOM still holds the whole title and the link's accessible name
      is the full product name even when the visible text is cut.
    - The price and the button are pinned to the bottom with margin-top:auto, NOT
      by reserving a fixed title height. That is what keeps prices on one line
      across a row of mixed one- and two-line titles.
    - The promo label sits on the image under the SALE badge, in the same stack, so
      a card with no sale still puts the offer at the top left.

  The class is `pcard prodcard`: .pcard carries the hover and quick-view rules it
  shares with the homepage category tiles, .prodcard is this card's own layout.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    A restricted product never gets a one-click add — the shopper is sent to the
    product page instead. See snippets/product-restricted.liquid.
  endcomment
  capture restricted
    render 'product-restricted', product: product
  endcapture
  assign restricted = restricted | strip

  comment
    Blank unless the price shown is genuinely reduced. The strikethrough and the
    SALE badge both hang off it — snippets/product-compare-at.liquid.
  endcomment
  capture was
    render 'product-compare-at', product: product
  endcapture
  assign was = was | strip

  capture promo
    render 'product-promo-label', product: product
  endcapture
  assign promo = promo | strip

  assign card_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  comment
    The collection grid's rule, which is the strict one: the rails used to ask only
    has_only_default_variant and would one-click add a product with a selling plan.
  endcomment
  assign quick_add = false
  if product.available and product.variants.size == 1 and product.selling_plan_groups.size == 0 and restricted != 'true'
    assign quick_add = true
  endif

  capture card_url
    render 'product-card-url', product: product
  endcapture
  assign card_url = card_url | strip
-%}
<div class="pcard prodcard"{% if width != blank %} style="flex:0 0 {{ width }};"{% endif %}>
  <div class="pcard-img prodcard-img">
    {%- if was != blank or promo != blank -%}
      <div class="prodcard-badges">
        {%- if was != blank -%}<span class="sale-badge">SALE</span>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if promo != blank -%}<span class="promo-label">{{ promo }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%} A div holds the link rather than being it: the quick-view eye is a
        button and cannot be nested inside an anchor. {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="{{ card_url }}" class="prodcard-imglink">
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        {%- capture card_alt %}{% render 'image-alt', image: product.featured_image, product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
        {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag: alt: card_alt, loading: 'lazy' }}
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="prodcard-ph"><span>image</span></span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>
    {% render 'wishlist-button', product: product %}
    {% render 'quick-view-button', product: product, restricted: restricted %}
  </div>
  <div class="prodcard-vendor">{{ product.vendor }}</div>
  <h3 class="prodcard-title"><a href="{{ card_url }}" class="hov-green">{{ product.title }}</a></h3>
  <div class="prodcard-rating">{% render 'product-rating', product: product, size: 14 %}</div>
  <div class="prodcard-foot">
    <span class="prodcard-price">{% if product.price_varies %}From {% endif %}{{ product.price | money }}</span>
    {%- if was != blank -%}<span class="price-was">{{ was }}</span>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- if quick_add -%}
    <button type="button" data-add-id="{{ card_variant.id }}" class="btn-sm btn-fill prodcard-cta">Add To Bag</button>
  {%- else -%}
    <a href="{{ card_url }}" class="btn-sm btn-fill prodcard-cta">View Product</a>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
